Z||000000||kornholio||04-16-2000||07:34 PM||||It's time to sell my 86 SE.  Could you tell me what it's worth?<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero1_1.jpg">  <P>179000 km (about 110000 miles)<BR>2.8L V6 automatic<BR>power windows<BR>power locks<BR>power trunk<BR>rear defogger<BR>tilt steering<BR>5 star rims<BR>2 sets of tires<BR>remote starter<BR>alarm<BR>keyless entry<BR>fog Lights<BR>CD player <BR>Pioneer speakers<BR>tinted windows<P>NEW:<BR>EGR tube, valve and solenoid<BR>battery<BR>thermostat<BR>brakes<BR>front tie-rods<BR>windshield wiper motor<BR>headlight motors<BR>catalytic convertor<BR>E-brake<BR>oxygen sensor<BR>throttle position sensor<P>tune-up in September: fuel filter, spark plugs, spark plug wires,distributor cap and rotor, air filter, pcv valve,<P>replaced alternator and belt<BR>front wheels aligned<p>[This message has been edited by kornholio (edited 04-16-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GT||04-16-2000||09:13 PM||||Sounds like its a well cared for car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  In my opinion, it should sell anywhere from 2 to 3K.  Try going to <A HREF="http://www.kelleybluebook.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kelleybluebook.com</A>  and see what its worth. I hope thats the right address||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||04-16-2000||09:59 PM||||Sounds like you have taken a lot of time to keep it in good shape.  It also looks very good.  I'd say you could get in the ballpark of $2500 (US).  With the V6, it gives it a higher value, but you may have to wait for someone who REALLY wants a Fiero to get top dollar.  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||04-16-2000||10:52 PM||||The kelly Blue Book website is <A HREF="http://www.kbb.com." TARGET=_blank>www.kbb.com.</A> <BR>or you could go to: <A HREF="http://www.xnet.com/~paulv/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xnet.com/~paulv/</A> <BR>This is the creator of the Fiero Price Guide. He rates the cars by keeping track of what the vehicles really sell for and figures out costthat way.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||04-17-2000||06:44 PM||||If you go  to the FOCONE web page there is a hot button for price estimations for Fieros.  Mostly set up for stock Fiero pricing. Any special modifications on your car become subjective as to worth.  It ends up that any car is worth what anyone else will pay for it.  I have more invested in my cars than I can get out of them.  My intent is to enjoy them, not sell them.<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 04-17-2000).]||||reg||3
